Z||000018||watts||12-03-2001||05:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR>[B]Umm, DUH, why would you attach a hood strut to a piece of sheet metal?<P> BTW the previously mentioned strut does work good when properly supported. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you refer to the thread that started all this, you'll see that it stated quite clearly to use the bracket that your cruise wiring would attach to.  It wouldn't have a hope in hell with a new strut, mounted to that point.  This would explain why we've both gone out and made (or bought) brackets.  <P>To any others who might not be quite as in the 'know' or have such facilities to manufacture/fabricate there own bracket I present....  The first post in this thread!  <P>You have a strut that works - I have a strut that works.  If someone else really wants, I'll make up all the parts I used (again) and ship it off to them if they are in the exact same boat I was.  Say $35us + shipping?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||jelly2m8||12-03-2001||05:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by watts:<BR>[B] If you refer to the thread that started all this, you'll see that it stated quite clearly to use the bracket that your cruise wiring would attach to.  It wouldn't have a hope in hell with a new strut, mounted to that point.  This would explain why we've both gone out and made (or bought) brackets.  <BR>  <P>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Woops, Guess I'm the guilty party here, I didn't look at that pasted URL. Your right.<P> Then again common sense tells me not to attach a deck/hood strut to a sheet metal bracket designed to support a few wires.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||RedOktober||12-03-2001||06:05 PM||||Jelly2m8.. did you drill into you strut tower to mount the lower barcket??? I'M sure it would be possible to do that. instead of using the tin bracket..<P>Do you still have your original springs on the trunk? cuz from the looks of it Watts still has his in.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||jelly2m8||12-03-2001||06:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RedOktober:<BR><B>Jelly2m8.. did you drill into you strut tower to mount the lower barcket??? I'M sure it would be possible to do that. instead of using the tin bracket..<P>Do you still have your original springs on the trunk? cuz from the looks of it Watts still has his in.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> Hey bud,<P>  Nope, my strut has the bracket welded to the decklid vent support. LMK if you want any close up pics.<P> I removed both decklid springs, the right side had to come out as it would have interfeared with the Plenum on my motor.<P> Good pick up on watts still having his decklid springs in. I missed it, the bracket nearly made me fall out of my seat, I didnt look at much else.<BR> Too bad he went thru all the fuss, when a simple adjustment probably would have fixed his prob... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>....throwing more fuel on the fire.....<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
